          "mdr_text_key": "16128963597",
          "text_type_code": "Description of Event or Problem",
          "patient_sequence_number": "0",
          "text": "It was reported that pump issued occlusion alarms resulting in the customer going to the emergency room the next date, (b)(6) 2026. The customer was admitted to the hospital's intensive care unit with a blood glucose level of 426 mg/dL, a healthcare provider identified ketone level as dangerous or life threatening. Customer was treated with intravenous fluids of saline and insulin which resolved the issue. The customer was released the same day with issue resolved and no permanent damage. Customer reported using the same cartridge for more than 48 hours and received education from Technical Support to change cartridge every 48 hours with Humalog brand insulin, after which case was closed."
